    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Choropleth maps in R with canvasXpress\"\ndescription: \"Color a world map by a value per country in R with canvasXpress — join your data to a topoJSON by name and get an interactive, reproducible choropleth.\"\nauthor: \"Isaac Neuhaus\"\ndate: \"2026-10-06\"\ncategories: [R, canvasXpress, maps, choropleth, visualization]\nimage: \"thumbnail.png\"\n---\n\n\n\nA choropleth map shades each region by a value — emissions, population, votes, incidence. The\ntrick is always the same: join a table of values to a set of map shapes by a common key, then\npick a color scale. In this post we build one in R with [canvasXpress](https://canvasxpress.org):\nyou pass a named vector of values and a topoJSON of boundaries, and the join and coloring happen\ninside the render, so the result is interactive and fully reproducible from a single spec.\n\n## One value per region\n\nA choropleth needs exactly one measurement per shape. In canvasXpress the **columns** are the\nregions (they match the map by name) and the **row** is the variable you color by — here CO₂\nemissions per country for 2018. We'll load a prepared table; swap it for your own (any\n`country → value` table works).\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(canvasXpress)\n\ny <- read.table(\n  \"https://www.canvasxpress.org/data/r/cX-CO2-dat.txt\",\n  header = TRUE, sep = \"\\t\", quote = \"\", row.names = 1,\n  check.names = FALSE, stringsAsFactors = FALSE\n)\n\ndim(y)              # 1 row (CO2) x N countries\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1]   1 198\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ny[, 1:4]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n    Afghanistan  Albania  Algeria Andorra\nCO2    10.45267 5.402999 164.3093 0.46421\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\nThe single row is the variable (`CO2`); each column name is a country that must match a shape in\nthe map. An optional **sample annotation** table (rows = countries) rides along for richer\ntooltips and legends — here the continent and ISO code.\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nx <- read.table(\n  \"https://www.canvasxpress.org/data/r/cX-CO2-smp.txt\",\n  header = TRUE, sep = \"\\t\", quote = \"\", row.names = 1,\n  check.names = FALSE, stringsAsFactors = FALSE\n)\nhead(x)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n            Code     Continent     Country\nAfghanistan  AFG          Asia Afghanistan\nAlbania      ALB        Europe     Albania\nAlgeria      DZA        Africa     Algeria\nAndorra      AND        Europe     Andorra\nAngola       AGO        Africa      Angola\nAnguilla     AIA North America    Anguilla\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n## The map\n\n`graphType = \"Map\"` with a `topoJSON` of world boundaries draws the shapes; `colorBy = \"CO2\"`\nshades each country by its value. The countries join to the map by name — no manual merge, no\nprojection math.\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ncanvasXpress(\n  data     = y,\n  smpAnnot = x,\n  graphType = \"Map\",\n  colorBy   = \"CO2\",\n  topoJSON  = \"https://www.canvasxpress.org/data/maps/WORLD.json\",\n  mapId     = \"countries\",\n  legendPosition = \"left\",\n  theme = \"solarized\",\n  title = \"CO2 Emissions per Country (2018)\",\n  width  = 700,\n  height = 500\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"htmlwidget-70a823243db4f9593073\" style=\"width:100%;height:464px;\" class=\"canvasXpress html-widget\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-70a823243db4f9593073\">{\"x\":{\"data\":{\"y\":{\"vars\":[\"CO2\"],\"smps\":[\"Afghanistan\",\"Albania\",\"Algeria\",\"Andorra\",\"Angola\",\"Anguilla\",\"Antigua & Barbuda\",\"Argentina\",\"Armenia\",\"Aruba\",\"Australia\",\"Austria\",\"Azerbaijan\",\"Bahamas\",\"Bahrain\",\"Bangladesh\",\"Barbados\",\"Belarus\",\"Belgium\",\"Belize\",\"Benin\",\"Bermuda\",\"Bhutan\",\"Bolivia\",\"Bosnia and Herzegovina\",\"Botswana\",\"Brazil\",\"British Virgin Islands\",\"Brunei Darussalam\",\"Bulgaria\"